<title>JAPAN: Japan's 1996 oil product output down 0.9 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan's 1996 oil product output down 0.9 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan produced 225.4 million kilolitres (kl) of oil products in 1996, down 0.9 percent from a year earlier, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It was the first year in nine years that Japan's oil production declined.</p>
<p>A trade ministry official said the decline was partly due to moves by oil companies to cut costs by keeping oil product inventories low.</p>
<p>&quot;(Japanese oil companies) want to avoid holding surplus stockpiles of oil products and the figures testify to that,&quot; he said.</p>
</text>
